  "notes": "Pattern B / brand-new -- University Park has no separate Psychology B.A. or B.S. degree-plan file built in this repo at all (checked: no PSYCH-*.json anywhere in degree_plans/), so there is no UP sibling to compare against; this is Behrend's own real, independently-researched curriculum, confirmed 2026-08-27 via direct fetch of bulletins.psu.edu/undergraduate/colleges/behrend/psychology-ba/. No 'BH' suffix applied to the code (unlike the other five majors in this batch) since there's no existing UP 'PSYCH' code to disambiguate from -- same plain-code convention already used elsewhere in this repo for majors that exist at only one non-UP campus (e.g. SUR-2026.json at Wilkes-Barre, ESUS-2026.json at World Campus). Real major structure (52cr): Prescribed Courses (PSYCH 100, 301W, 406W, 489 -- 12cr), Additional Required Courses (ENGL 15/30H, PSYCH 200 or STAT 200, CAS 100A/B/C, ENGL 202A/B/C/D -- 13cr), Content Area Requirements ('select 3 credits from 4 of 5 categories' -- 12cr), and Supporting Courses (Practicum/Internship/Research from PSYCH 294/296/494/495/496 -- 3cr; Additional 200/300/400-level Psychology -- 3cr; 400-level Psychology excluding 494-496 -- 9cr). The engine has no mechanism to model 'choose 4 of 5 categories' (every plan item is a required slot) -- modeled the four most commonly required content areas (Biological Bases of Behavior, Social/Developmental, Cognitive/Learning, Clinical/Applied), omitting Diversity (the smallest of the five pools), and documenting that simplification here rather than silently guessing which 4 a real student would pick. Real category course lists, confirmed verbatim from the bulletin: Biological Bases (PSYCH 253/260/269), Social/Developmental (HDFS 129/229, PSYCH 212/221), Cognitive/Learning (PSYCH 256/261/263N/268), Clinical/Applied (EDPSY 14, PSYCH 217N/238/243/244/270/281). B.A.-specific requirements (24cr): World Language (0-12cr, modeled as 3 generic Level 1/2/3 slots), B.A. Fields (9cr, 3 slots), World Cultures (0-3cr, 1 slot). Total minimum degree credits per the bulletin: 120. Entrance to major requires 2.0 GPA and third-semester classification, not modeled directly (same limitation as every other major's GPA/classification entrance requirement in this repo).",
